OneDrive client
---------------

Work in progress. See PLAN.md in this directory for the design and for how to
create the Microsoft Entra tenant and app that provide the credentials.

Current state:

- OAuth works (personal Microsoft accounts only): the dashboard `/redirect`
  route sends the user to Microsoft, `/clients/onedrive/authenticate` (site
  route) checks the `state` cookie and hands the code to the dashboard
  `/authenticate` route, which exchanges it for tokens, reads the account
  from Graph, and saves it (`database.js`) and sets `blog.client`.
- `util/getAccessToken.js` returns a valid access token, refreshing and
  saving the rotated tokens; a rejected refresh token sets `error_code` 401,
  and the dashboard shows a reconnect prompt.
- After connecting, `setup.js` (under the folder lock) creates a folder named
  after the blog inside the app folder (`Apps/<app name>/<blog title>`, renamed
  automatically if taken) and uploads the blog's files with
  `sync/reset-from-blot.js`. Progress shows through the sync status.
- `write` and `remove` change the local folder and OneDrive. Before the
  OneDrive folder exists they only change the local folder.
- `resync` is `sync/reset-to-blot.js` (OneDrive -> Blot, used by the dashboard's
  reset tools); `sync/reset-from-blot.js` is the reverse (Blot -> OneDrive).
- `getHealth` reports REAUTH_REQUIRED (access revoked / refresh token
  rejected), SOURCE_MISSING (folder deleted) and QUOTA_EXCEEDED (storage full)
  from `error_code` on the stored account, set by `util/persistError.js` using
  the rules in `util/classifyError.js`. Transient errors (throttling, 5xx) are
  retried in `util/graph.js` and never reported as health issues.
- `disconnect` clears `blog.client` and forgets the stored tokens (it does not
  delete the user's OneDrive folder).
- `site_routes` also exposes `POST /webhook`, which answers Graph's
  `validationToken` handshake, checks `clientState` on notifications and
  responds 202, but does not act on them.
- The client is only registered (`app/clients/index.js`) once
  `config.onedrive.{client_id,client_secret,webhook_secret}` are set.

Not implemented: pulling changes from OneDrive automatically (delta sync),
Graph change-notification subscriptions and renewal, a polling fallback. Until
then changes made in OneDrive only reach Blot via the dashboard's resync. Do
not set the credentials in production until delta sync exists. If setup fails
part way the sync status shows the error; the user can disconnect and retry.
